Description: Build the bundled oniguruma of ext/mbstring when the oniguruma package is installed (7.4 and 8.x need it): the package's oniguruma.h 6.x in /usr/local/include came before the bundled 5.9 headers in the include path, and php_mbregex.c did not compile ("incomplete definition of type 'php_mb_regex_t'"). The bundled headers now go first.
Origin: azsupport; found by the FreeBSD 15.1 build test, PHP_ADD_INCLUDE(dir, 1) prepends

diff --git a/ext/mbstring/config.m4 b/ext/mbstring/config.m4
index 25bf23876..e60b18926 100644
--- a/ext/mbstring/config.m4
+++ b/ext/mbstring/config.m4
@@ -38,9 +38,11 @@ AC_DEFUN([PHP_MBSTRING_EXTENSION], [
     PHP_ADD_BUILD_DIR([$ext_builddir/$dir], 1)
   done
   
+  dnl The bundled headers go first: with the oniguruma package installed, its
+  dnl oniguruma.h in /usr/local/include would otherwise shadow the bundled one.
   for dir in $PHP_MBSTRING_EXTRA_INCLUDES; do
-    PHP_ADD_INCLUDE([$ext_srcdir/$dir])
-    PHP_ADD_INCLUDE([$ext_builddir/$dir])
+    PHP_ADD_INCLUDE([$ext_srcdir/$dir], 1)
+    PHP_ADD_INCLUDE([$ext_builddir/$dir], 1)
   done
 
   if test "$ext_shared" = "no"; then
